{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794604581,"nonce":"sHhvlmis+ilrC1i0dZrB/jd5F1E=","title":"HashLink bindings on Android and iOS through Ash","message":"Ash (from 12dbd2e5 on its main, not yet released) links a HashLink program for Android and iOS with `ash --build --target \u003ctriple\u003e`, taking each native library as a static archive with `--native-lib`, since a phone cannot open an HDLL. hxn's HashLink adapter is a Rust static library, so an hxn library could run on phones through Ash as it already does through hxcpp. Tried on 2026-11-13 with the generated counter fixture.\n\nWhat hxn needed, done in 38f3277: on a phone every library and the runtime are one link, so the resolver names must not collide. Every generated primitive is now named after its library (`hlp_counter_future_state`, via `@:hlNative(\"counter\", \"counter_\")`); before, `future_state` collided with ash_std's own `hlp_future_state`, and two hxn libraries would have collided with each other. Ash will make a primitive named like one of its runtime's `hlp_*` exports an explicit build error.\n\nWhat ran: with a source-built aarch64-linux-android runtime, hello-world and the generated counter fixture linked and ran under `adb shell` on the Pixel_9_Pro emulator up to the first forced collection, deliberate panic included; the collection crashed. That was Ash's (non-main threads on Android and iOS registered a guessed stack top), fixed in Ash bf070ca5. iOS simulator runtimes prepared by hand did not link (`_rust_eh_personality` undefined after Ash's localize script plus strip); Ash is replacing that script by isolating each Rust archive's internals at link time, which in its current in-progress binary fails on Android with \"-r and -pie may not be used together\" (reported).\n\nStill to do once Ash pushes and releases that work:\n- Run the generated counter fixture and the examples on the Android emulator and the iOS simulator.\n- Build the adapter for a phone triple from the command: `hxn build hl --target \u003candroid or ios triple\u003e` producing the static archive, and `tests/mobile/run.sh` modes for HashLink.\n- Document the phone build in the design and the testing guide.\n\nThe hand-written fixture under tests/counter/hl keeps unprefixed names (`hlp_future_state`), so it would still collide with ash_std's export on a phone; only the generated bindings are meant for phones.","files":null}]}